tasks.description:
In `web/src/main/scala/net/wiringbits/webapp/utils/slinkyUtils/compat/MuiCompat.scala`, add:
```scala
def freeSoloAutocompleteProps[T](
    options: Seq[T],
    renderInput: AutocompleteRenderInputParams => ReactElement,
    inputValue: String,
    getOptionLabel: js.Any => String,
    onSelect: js.Any => Unit,
    onInput: (String, String) => Unit,
    disabled: Boolean = false,
    fullWidth: Boolean = false
): AutocompleteProps[T, Boolean, Boolean, Boolean, "div"]
```

The body should:
- build `AutocompleteProps[T, Boolean, Boolean, Boolean, "div"](options = options.toJSArray, renderInput = renderInput)`;
- cast to `js.Dynamic` and set `freeSolo = true`, `size = "small"`, `inputValue`, and `getOptionLabel = (opt: js.Any) => getOptionLabel(opt)`;
- set `disabled` and `fullWidth` only when they are true. This keeps them undefined by default, like the existing `paginationProps` handling of `size`. MUI treats undefined and false the same;
- set `onChange = (_: js.Any, value: js.Any, _: js.Any, _: js.Any) => onSelect(value)`;
- set `onInputChange = (_: js.Any, value: js.Any, reason: js.Any) => { val (text, rsn) = autocompleteInputChange(value = value, reason = reason); onInput(text, rsn) }`;
- return the typed props.

Add imports for `AutocompleteProps`, `slinky.core.facade.ReactElement` and `scala.scalajs.js.JSConverters.*`. Add a short comment saying why the dynamic mutation is needed: ScalablyTyped does not expose these props.

Extend `web/src/test/scala/net/wiringbits/webapp/utils/slinkyUtils/compat/MuiCompatSpec.scala` with a `"freeSoloAutocompleteProps" should { ... }` block in the existing style, reading fields through `asInstanceOf[js.Dynamic]` as the pagination tests do. Cover:
- freeSolo is true, size is "small", and inputValue passes through;
- options length is right;
- disabled and fullWidth are undefined by default and true when passed true;
- getOptionLabel delegates;
- calling `onChange` as a `js.Function4` forwards the raw value to onSelect;
- calling `onInputChange` as a `js.Function3` with ("abc", "input") gives onInput ("abc", "input"), and with non-string values gives ("", "").

Use simple options such as `Seq("a", "b")` and `renderInput = _ => Fragment()` or similar. Pass every argument by name.

In `docs/guide/frontend.md`:
- **RULE-FE-012**: replace the `acProps` + `dyn.*` mutation part of the example (from `val acProps = ...` through the `onInputChange` block) with one call to `MuiCompat.freeSoloAutocompleteProps(...)` using named args. The example should keep the `(value: Any) match` inside `onSelect` and keep the `reason != "reset"` handling inside `onInput`. Keep the `myOptionLabel` explanation.
- Reword the "`js.Dynamic` mutation" key-rule bullet: the cast-and-mutate lives only in this helper; pages must not repeat it. Shapes the helper doesn't cover (e.g. value-controlled, non-freeSolo, extra props) still build `AutocompleteProps` directly.
- Change the `@file:` reference line to a site that will use the helper: `web/src/main/scala/net/wiringbits/components/pages/bankstatementreview/BankRowRuleForm.scala`.
- Add a row to the RULE-FE-014 helper table: `Free-solo Autocomplete props | MuiCompat.freeSoloAutocompleteProps(...)`.
- Do not renumber or edit other rules.

Verify with `CI=true sbt Test/compile`, then `sbt "web/testOnly *MuiCompatSpec"`. Node 24 must be on PATH for web tests.
